From: Claude
Subject: [PATCH] ci(claude-review): allow claude[bot] as triggering actor

Pushes by claude[bot] on a PR fire the pull_request: synchronize event,
which re-runs anthropics/claude-code-action@v1. Because allowed_bots
defaults to "" (no bots permitted), the action fails with:

  Workflow initiated by non-human actor: claude (type: Bot).
  Add bot to allowed_bots list or use '*' to allow all bots.

Allow only claude[bot] (not all bots) so re-runs caused by Claude's
own commits succeed without broadening the trust boundary.

---
 .github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml b/.github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml
--- a/.github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/claude-code-review.yml
@@ -39,5 +39,6 @@ jobs:
           plugin_marketplaces: 'https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code.git'
           plugins: 'code-review@claude-code-plugins'
           prompt: '/code-review:code-review ${{ github.repository }}/pull/${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}'
+          allowed_bots: 'claude[bot]'
           # See https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code-action/blob/main/docs/usage.md
           # or https://code.claude.com/docs/en/cli-reference for available options
